  "notes": "University Park. PNG 490 (capstone) genuinely requires all of PNG 430, PNG 440W, PNG 450, EME 460, PNG 475, and GEOSC 454 completed first (a real AND-chain, not a flattened OR artifact) \u2014 all six are already independently required elsewhere in this plan, so no extra items were needed. 'Technical Elective' pool is modeled generically. Post-parens-fix re-scrape (AND/OR prereq-parsing bug fix) revealed CHEM 110's and EME 210's real prereq is MATH 22 (previously empty) -- MATH 140/141 (this plan's own Calc I/II track) do NOT substitute for it -- and MATH 22 itself real-chains through MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3, none of which were in the plan. With CHEM 110 permanently stuck, CHEM 111/112 were also unschedulable, cascading to EME 301 (needs CHEM 112 AND PHYS 212 AND MATH 250/251, a real AND-chain) and PNG 480 (needs EME 301 AND EME 303 both, also a real AND-chain, not an OR as the flattened bug used to make it look), and PNG 482 (needs concurrent PNG 475 AND PNG 480). Added the real chain explicitly: MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3), MATH 22 (Semester 4) -- same convention used for LSCPE/ABSM/MATSCI's identical gap. The added 12cr didn't fit in 8 terms at the original 17cr/semester cap -- bumped max_credits_per_semester to 19 (the minimum that closes the gap) to keep 4-year graduation achievable.",
